  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the metallurgical extraction of copper, following reaction is used :</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>FeSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> respectively are.</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "gangue and flux.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "flux and slag",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "slag and flux.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Gauge and slag",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>During extraction of copper, iron oxide present as impurity is removed by adding <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and converting it into <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>FeSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Flux</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Slag</mi></math></p><p>Hence,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi></math>&nbsp;is gangue and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is slag.</p>"
  }
}